{"event":"trap-result","runId":"bugfix-direct-3","trapId":"bugfix-direct-3/trap-1","ordinal":1,"result":{"found":true,"rootCause":"The CLI's makeHost constructs a bare MockAdapter whose decide case returns the canned {choice:\"a\", confidence:0.9}. That matches none of the JudgeFixLoop decide options (revise/keep, update/keep, converged/continue), so the loop never revises and never converges — silently, with no error. The host suite works around it with host.setCanned(\"decide\", decideLocal); the CLI never wires it. The adapter's canned decide is deliberate (the swap test requires the host mock adapter to match the mock plugin byte-identically), so the fix belongs in the CLI, not the adapter.","file":"src/cli.ts","edits":[{"search":"import { compilerVersion } from \"./gate\";","replace":"import { compilerVersion } from \"./gate\";\nimport { decideLocal } from \"./decision-model\";"},{"search":"  if (adapterName === \"mock\") adapter = new MockAdapter({ gates });\n  else if (adapterName === \"direct\") adapter = new DirectAdapter();\n  else adapter = await Host.loadAdapter(adapterName);\n  return new Host({ stateDir: stateDir(args), adapter, clock });","replace":"  if (adapterName === \"mock\") adapter = new MockAdapter({ gates });\n  else if (adapterName === \"direct\") adapter = new DirectAdapter();\n  else adapter = await Host.loadAdapter(adapterName);\n  // BRA-54: the mock adapter's canned decide {choice:\"a\"} cannot\n  // answer revise/keep/converged questions, so the CLI mock path\n  // could not drive decide-heavy workflows (the JudgeFixLoop\n  // workflow looped 6 times unconverged, mean stuck at 0.55). Wire\n  // the local decision model in by default — a queued or setCanned\n  // answer still wins, since the adapter consults those first.\n  if (adapter instanceof MockAdapter) {\n    adapter.setCanned(\"decide\", (_type, arg) => ({ value: decideLocal(arg.question, arg.options) }));\n  }\n  return new Host({ stateDir: stateDir(args), adapter, clock });"}],"rationale":"Wire the local decision model into the CLI mock path by default: in makeHost, when the adapter is a MockAdapter, setCanned(\"decide\", decideLocal) — the same mechanism the host suite uses. Queued and setCanned answers are consulted before the adapter's switch, so an explicitly configured canned answer still wins. The adapter itself is untouched, so the swap test's byte-identical invariant and the trap-types canned expectations hold.","error":"","simulated":false}}
{"event":"trap","runId":"bugfix-direct-3","trapId":"bugfix-direct-3/trap-2","ordinal":2,"type":"job","arg":{"spec":"bugfix-fix","input":{"repoRoot":"/home/hatch/workspace/agentts-repo/apps/agentts","file":"src/cli.ts","edits":[{"search":"import { compilerVersion } from \"./gate\";","replace":"import { compilerVersion } from \"./gate\";\nimport { decideLocal } from \"./decision-model\";"},{"search":"  if (adapterName === \"mock\") adapter = new MockAdapter({ gates });\n  else if (adapterName === \"direct\") adapter = new DirectAdapter();\n  else adapter = await Host.loadAdapter(adapterName);\n  return new Host({ stateDir: stateDir(args), adapter, clock });","replace":"  if (adapterName === \"mock\") adapter = new MockAdapter({ gates });\n  else if (adapterName === \"direct\") adapter = new DirectAdapter();\n  else adapter = await Host.loadAdapter(adapterName);\n  // BRA-54: the mock adapter's canned decide {choice:\"a\"} cannot\n  // answer revise/keep/converged questions, so the CLI mock path\n  // could not drive decide-heavy workflows (the JudgeFixLoop\n  // workflow looped 6 times unconverged, mean stuck at 0.55). Wire\n  // the local decision model in by default — a queued or setCanned\n  // answer still wins, since the adapter consults those first.\n  if (adapter instanceof MockAdapter) {\n    adapter.setCanned(\"decide\", (_type, arg) => ({ value: decideLocal(arg.question, arg.options) }));\n  }\n  return new Host({ stateDir: stateDir(args), adapter, clock });"}]}}}
